===Phrase===
{{infl|en|phrase|head=[[his]] [[back]] [[is]] [[up]]}}

# {{idiomatic|1811}} he is offended or angry; an expression or idea taken from a cat; that animal, when angry, always raising its back. An allusion also sometimes used to jeer a crooked man; 
#:''So, Sir, I see somebody has offended you, for your '''back is up'''.''

